{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793854715,"nonce":"lf18CbsM/wdeKeDy1Qt467ITFxE=","title":"Dead-lettering a run after a poison launch leaves a unit with no recorded handle running","message":"Found by the correctness review of the e25c3b5 fix (AFK run 20261104-2224, branch fix/afk-open-bugs-2026-11-04). Not a regression; pre-existing.\n\nreconcile dead-letters a poison LAUNCH_STEP (dead_letter_outbox) before dead_letter_run. If that launch created the Pod but failed before set_attempt_handle (for example ensure_step_secrets failed after the create), dead_letter_run now writes a CANCEL_ATTEMPT through cancel_live_steps, but the teardown finds no handle and outbox_key_pending(launch:...) is false (dead-lettered rows are excluded), so it retires as Gone and no cancel is sent. The unit runs on.\n\nFix sketch: in dead_letter_run, for an in-flight attempt with no stored handle, record the backend's deterministic Executor::unit_handle as the attempt's handle before cancelling, as adopt_unit_of_refused_launch does (crates/scarab-engine/src/scheduler.rs). Test: World harness in crates/scarab-server/tests/redteam_open_bugs_final.rs: a launch that creates its unit then errors before the handle is recorded, poisoned to its ceiling; assert the unit is torn down.","files":null}]}